    {
      "id": "in-an",
      "title": "in or an",
      "level": "A2",
      "labels": ["in", "an"],
      "listen": "Both hum through the nose, but the mouth shape is different. For in your lips spread wide, almost a smile, and the sound is close to the \"a\" of \"cat\" pushed through the nose. For an the jaw drops and the sound is closer to \"ah\". Smile means in, open mouth means an.",
