      "title": "eu or ou",
      "level": "A2",
      "labels": ["eu", "ou"],
      "listen": "Both are said with rounded lips, so you cannot go by rounding alone. For eu the mouth is relaxed and a little open, like the vowel in English \"her\" but with the lips pushed forward. For ou the lips close to a small tight hole and you get the \"oo\" of \"food\". Eu is open and soft, ou is tight and deep.",
